  "body": "﻿Answers the docs lane of #291 with two pieces, per the plan discussed there.\n\n**`examples/`** - a complete `first-part.camproj` the guide can teach on: our own clean-room flange fixture (model embedded as facets, so the file is self-contained), stock, Face / 2D Pocket / Drill with generated toolpaths, and the posted `first-part.nc`. Built end-to-end through the MCP server; verify is clean; it round-trips through File > Open.\n\n**`docs/images/first-part-*.png`** - four tutorial step pictures that are golden files, not hand-captured screenshots. The docs test in `crates/ui/tests/gpu_render.rs` opens the project through the real open command, steps through `operation_order`, and renders each step with the real viewport pipelines and the real toolpath display (`interact::toolpath_lines`). A normal run compares and fails on drift; `UPDATE_DOCS_IMAGES=1` regenerates - same workflow as the kittest snapshots.\n\nNotes:\n- The test lives in the existing `gpu_render` binary on purpose: it shares that binary's GPU lock and adds no new test process (a fifth process racing fallback-device creation across processes is what makes full-suite runs flake).\n- While in there, the binary now renders every frame on one shared `OnceLock` device instead of one per frame - the per-frame create/teardown churn was the flake hazard; readbacks are identical and the binary got ~3.5x faster.\n- `interact::toolpath_lines`: `pub(crate)` -> `pub` so the test draws through the app's own path display.\n\nTest stability: `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --test gpu_render` is 10/10 across repeated runs and deterministic through a regen/compare round-trip. The full-suite wgpu flake is pre-existing on `main` (untouched baseline crashed 3 of 4 runs on this machine) and unrelated to this change.\n\nKeeping this draft until the open questions in #291 are answered - images can move to `docs/guide/src/images/` when the mdbook scaffold lands.\r\n",
